<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ lang or summit.lang }}">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">

<title>{% if title %}{{ title }} | {{ summit.shortName }}{% else %}{{ summit.name }} — {{ summit.tagline }}{% endif %}</title>
<meta name="description" content="{{ description }}">
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ page.url | absoluteUrl }}">
<link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="{{ basePath | absoluteUrl }}">
<link rel="alternate" hreflang="zh-Hans" href="{{ ("/zh" + basePath) | absoluteUrl }}">
<link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="{{ basePath | absoluteUrl }}">
{% if translationStatus == "machine" %}<meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">{% endif %}

<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ summit.name }}">
<meta property="og:title" content="{% if title %}{{ title }}{% else %}{{ summit.name }}{% endif %}">
<meta property="og:description" content="{{ description }}">
<meta property="og:url" content="{{ page.url | absoluteUrl }}">
<meta property="og:locale" content="en_KE">
<meta property="og:image" content="{{ '/img/logo-600.jpg' | absoluteUrl }}">
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">

<link rel="icon" href="/img/emblem-96.png" type="image/png">
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/img/apple-touch-icon.png">

{# The two faces that render the first viewport. Preloaded so the masthead and
   the engraved h1 never swap; Courier and the heavier Archivo weights can. #}
<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/bricolage-grotesque.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/google-sans-flex.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
{% if basePath == "/" %}<link rel="preload" as="image" href="/img/hero-poster.avif" type="image/avif" fetchpriority="high">{% endif %}

<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/tokens.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">

{% block head %}{% endblock %}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "ConferenceEvent",
  "name": {{ summit.name | dump | safe }},
  "description": {{ summit.theme | dump | safe }},
  "startDate": "{{ summit.dates.start }}",
  "endDate": "{{ summit.dates.end }}",
  "eventStatus": "https://schema.org/EventScheduled",
  "eventAttendanceMode": "https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode",
  "url": {{ summit.url | dump | safe }},
  "location": {
    "@type": "Place",
    "name": {{ summit.location.venue | dump | safe }},
    "address": {
      "@type": "PostalAddress",
      "streetAddress": {{ summit.location.street | dump | safe }},
      "addressLocality": {{ summit.location.city | dump | safe }},
      "addressCountry": {{ summit.location.countryCode | dump | safe }}
    }
  },
  "organizer": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": {{ summit.organiser.name | dump | safe }},
    "url": {{ summit.organiser.url | dump | safe }},
    "email": {{ summit.contact.email | dump | safe }},
    "telephone": {{ summit.contact.phone | dump | safe }}
  }
}
</script>
</head>

<body>
<!--
DIRECTION CONTRACT · seed 14313fed · persuade · grounded candidate 4 of 7

THESIS: This summit exists to move Kenyan tea into Chinese markets at better value.
The site takes its visual register from the security printing that surrounds that
trade — but it is no longer written as a document. It refuses the generic conference
template (speaker grid, sponsor wall, stock delegates mid-handshake) and its
cream-editorial opposite. It does carry a video hero and a countdown, added in the
hero refresh; the earlier version of this contract said it refused those, and that
sentence outlived the decision.

OWN-WORLD: Security print, visual register only. Intaglio green ground owning whole
regions, green-grey safety-tint stock (never cream), oxblood for emphasis, canary and
salmon plies. Generated guilloche rosette and engine-turned rules. Bricolage Grotesque
display, Google Sans Flex UI, Google Sans Code typed data. Photographic plate grids.
The DOCUMENT VOCABULARY was removed in ADR-015 after the client's copy audit — no
schedule names, no serials, no unstamped fields. The look is the world now, not the
labels.

STORY: A buyer weighing an unfamiliar summit reads a page that is confident about what
is settled and plain about what is not, and registers interest.

FIRST VIEWPORT: Full-bleed intaglio ground over the plantation video, rosette bleeding
off the right edge. Plain h1 left; the particulars beneath as label/value fields, with
unannounced values reading "To be announced". Registration panel right, on light stock,
carrying the primary action.

FORM: Security-printed certificate — as a visual register only. The bill-of-lading
voice that once came with it was removed in ADR-015. Ranked 4 of 7; assigned by the roll.

FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md
-->
<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to main content</a>

{# Top bar. The four facts a visitor arrives wanting, above everything else.
   The day count renders server-side via the daysUntil filter so it is present
   with JS off; hero.js re-reads [data-countdown] and corrects it against the
   visitor's clock rather than the build clock. #}
<div class="topbar">
  <p class="topbar__inner">
    <span class="topbar__when"><strong>{{ summit.dates.display }}</strong></span>
    <span class="topbar__dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
    <span>{{ summit.location.venueShort }}, {{ summit.location.city }}</span>
    <span class="topbar__dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
    <span class="topbar__open">Registration open</span>
    <span class="topbar__dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
    <span class="topbar__count"><strong data-countdown="{{ summit.dates.start }}">{{ summit.dates.start | daysUntil }}</strong> days to go</span>
  </p>
</div>

<header class="site-header">
  <a class="site-header__brand" href="/" aria-label="{{ summit.name }} — home">
    <img class="brand-emblem" src="/img/emblem-96.png" srcset="/img/emblem-96.png 96w, /img/emblem-256.png 256w"
         sizes="44px" width="96" height="96" alt="" decoding="async">
    <span class="brand-lockup">
      <span class="brand-lockup__title">Kenya&#8202;/&#8202;China</span>
      <span class="brand-lockup__sub">Tea Summit</span>
    </span>
  </a>

  <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Primary">
    <button class="site-nav__toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="primary-nav">
      <span class="visually-hidden">Menu</span>
      <span class="site-nav__bars" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </button>
    <ul class="site-nav__list" id="primary-nav">
      {% for item in navigation.primary %}
      {# Compare basePath, not page.url — under /zh/ the two never match. #}
      <li{% if item.children %} class="has-sub"{% endif %}>
        <a href="{{ item.url }}"{% if item | inSection(basePath) %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ item.text }}</a>
        {%- if item.children %}
        {# CSS-only submenu: opened by :hover and :focus-within, so it works for
           keyboard users with no JS. On narrow screens it renders inline and
           always open, which is why there is no aria-expanded to keep in sync. #}
        <ul class="site-nav__sub">
          {% for child in item.children %}
          <li><a href="{{ child.url }}"{% if basePath == child.url %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ child.text }}</a></li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
        {%- endif %}
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {# data-nolocale: the one link that must NOT be rewritten to the current
       locale, since crossing locales is its whole job. See the localeLinks
       transform in eleventy.config.js. #}
    <a class="lang-switch" data-nolocale
       href="{% if locale == 'zh' %}{{ basePath }}{% else %}/zh{{ basePath }}{% endif %}"
       lang="{% if locale == 'zh' %}en{% else %}zh-Hans{% endif %}"
       rel="alternate"
       hreflang="{% if locale == 'zh' %}en{% else %}zh-Hans{% endif %}">{% if locale == 'zh' %}English{% else %}中文{% endif %}</a>
  </nav>

  <a class="btn btn--primary site-header__cta" href="{{ navigation.cta.url }}">{{ navigation.cta.text }}</a>
</header>

<main id="main">
  {{ content | safe }}
</main>

<footer class="site-footer">
  <div class="site-footer__grid">
    {% for group in navigation.footer %}
    <nav class="site-footer__col" aria-labelledby="foot-{{ loop.index }}">
      <h2 class="site-footer__heading" id="foot-{{ loop.index }}">{{ group.heading }}</h2>
      <ul>
        {% for link in group.links %}
        <li><a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.text }}</a></li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </nav>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <div class="site-footer__base">
    <p>{{ summit.name }} &middot; {{ summit.dates.display }} &middot; {{ summit.location.venueShort }}, {{ summit.location.city }}</p>
    <p>Organised by {{ summit.organiser.legalEntity }}{% if summit.partners.length %}, in partnership with {% for p in summit.partners %}{{ p.name }}{% if not loop.last %} and {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}.</p>
    {# No postal address here. The only address the site states is the venue —
       see the note on summit.contact in src/_data/summit.js. #}
    <p>{{ summit.location.venue }}, {{ summit.location.street }}, {{ summit.location.city }} &middot; <a href="tel:{{ summit.contact.phone | replace(" ", "") }}">{{ summit.contact.phone }}</a></p>
    <p><a href="mailto:{{ summit.contact.email }}">{{ summit.contact.email }}</a></p>
    <p class="site-footer__legal">{% for l in navigation.legal %}<a href="{{ l.url }}">{{ l.text }}</a>{% if not loop.last %} &middot; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>
    <p>&copy; {{ buildYear }} {{ summit.organiser.legalEntity }}. All rights reserved.</p>
  </div>
</footer>

{# WhatsApp, not a chat widget. The number takes calls and messages, so this is
   a real channel rather than a bot. Crucially it is a plain link: no
   third-party script, no cookie, which is what keeps the site free of a
   consent banner. See docs/V3-SCOPE.md. #}
<a class="wa-float" href="https://wa.me/{{ summit.contact.whatsapp }}"
   target="_blank" rel="noopener"
   aria-label="Chat with the summit team on WhatsApp">
  <svg class="wa-float__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    <path fill="currentColor" d="M12.04 2C6.58 2 2.13 6.45 2.13 11.91c0 1.75.46 3.45 1.32 4.95L2 22l5.25-1.38a9.9 9.9 0 0 0 4.79 1.22h.01c5.46 0 9.91-4.45 9.91-9.91 0-2.65-1.03-5.14-2.9-7.01A9.82 9.82 0 0 0 12.04 2Zm0 18.15h-.01a8.2 8.2 0 0 1-4.19-1.15l-.3-.18-3.12.82.83-3.04-.2-.31a8.19 8.19 0 0 1-1.26-4.38c0-4.54 3.7-8.24 8.25-8.24a8.2 8.2 0 0 1 8.24 8.25c0 4.54-3.7 8.23-8.24 8.23Zm4.52-6.16c-.25-.12-1.47-.72-1.69-.81-.23-.08-.39-.12-.56.13-.16.24-.64.8-.78.97-.15.16-.29.18-.54.06-.25-.13-1.05-.39-1.99-1.23-.74-.66-1.23-1.47-1.38-1.72-.14-.25-.01-.38.11-.5.11-.11.25-.29.37-.44.13-.15.17-.25.25-.42.08-.16.04-.31-.02-.43-.06-.12-.56-1.34-.76-1.84-.2-.48-.4-.42-.56-.43h-.47c-.16 0-.43.06-.65.31-.22.25-.85.83-.85 2.03s.87 2.35.99 2.51c.12.16 1.71 2.61 4.14 3.66.58.25 1.03.4 1.38.51.58.19 1.11.16 1.53.1.47-.07 1.47-.6 1.67-1.18.21-.58.21-1.07.15-1.18-.06-.11-.22-.17-.47-.29Z"/>
  </svg>
  <span class="wa-float__label">Chat on WhatsApp</span>
</a>

<script src="/js/nav.js" defer></script>
<script src="/js/form-handler.js" defer></script>
<script src="/js/hero.js" defer></script>
{# Turnstile. Without this the .cf-turnstile div in the forms renders nothing,
   no cf-turnstile-response token is produced, and every genuine submission
   scores a turnstile failure. Loaded only when a real site key exists, so a
   misconfigured build ships no widget rather than a broken one.
   challenges.cloudflare.com is already allowed in script-src and frame-src. #}
{% if turnstileSiteKey %}<script src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js" defer></script>{% endif %}
{% block scripts %}{% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
